%% title: Manual feed success - web to device with ack
%% source: dashboard/commands.py:34-73 send_command, BEGIN IMMEDIATE and publish
%% source: dashboard/handlers.py:118-147 handle_ack, db.py:414-440 apply_ack

sequenceDiagram
  participant OP as Operator
  participant CP as Control page
  participant SC as commands.send_command
  participant DB as DB SQLite
  participant B as Broker
  participant ESP as ESP32

  OP->>CP: enter portions 2 and press feed
  CP->>CP: confirm dialog, shows ack timeout 30 s
  OP->>CP: confirm
  CP->>SC: client_command manual_feed with portions 2
  SC->>DB: ensure_device feeder-64008c
  SC->>DB: BEGIN IMMEDIATE
  SC->>DB: INSERT commands, status sent
  SC->>DB: INSERT feeding_logs, status pending, level before
  SC->>DB: COMMIT
  SC->>B: publish command QoS 1, command_id cmd-...
  SC-->>CP: command_id and feed_log_id
  CP-->>OP: toast command sent
  B-->>ESP: command manual_feed portions 2
  ESP->>ESP: guards pass, phase idle, servo ready, level above 0
  ESP->>ESP: feedStart portions 2
  loop once per portion
    ESP->>ESP: servo open, open phase 1000 ms
    ESP->>ESP: servo close, settle 300 ms, jobRemaining decrement
    ESP->>ESP: gap 200 ms before the next portion
  end
  ESP->>ESP: finishFeed, measure distance
  ESP->>B: publish telemetry with post-feed level
  ESP->>B: publish ack result ok, message feeding 2 portions
  B-->>DB: worker handle_ack then apply_ack
  DB->>DB: commands status success, acked_at set
  DB->>DB: feeding_logs status success
  DB->>DB: attach_feed_level_after from latest telemetry
  CP->>DB: data.status_of and recent_commands, cache TTL 2 s
  DB-->>CP: status success
  CP-->>OP: history row shows success
  Note over SC,DB: rows are written before publish, so any late ack still correlates
